  CSS rules pulled (source/css/external-00-base.css + external-01-slick.css):
    .new-banner-home (13 rules), .new_banner_contant (11), .banner-list (3),
    .banner-black-btn (2), .banner-shipping (4), .home--reivew (18),
    .review-content-item-tab/-top/-avatar/-content-yea/-bottom/-author/-stars,
    .verified-badge, .slider-main-part (29), .slick-dots/-track/-slide (slick.css base).

  Hero font (source actual): Circular Std Medium 500 (paid Linotype, loaded inline
    via @font-face from cdn.shopify.com/s/files/.../circular-std-medium-500-webfont.woff2).
    Force-overrides theme via:
      body:not(:has(.gps)) h1,h2,h3,h4,h5,h6 { font-family:'circular_stdmedium' !important; }
    NOT available on Google Fonts (commercial license required to ship).
    Substitute: Inter (already wired in assets/bq-tokens.css). Plain weight 500,
    accent <strong> weight 700. Closest free equivalents in order: Manrope, Inter, Mona Sans.

  Slick carousel init (source script, hero only):
    $(...).slick({
      dots: true, arrows: false, infinite: true, slidesToShow: 1, slidesToScroll: 1,
      adaptiveHeight: true, speed: 300,
      // NO autoplay
      responsive: [{ breakpoint:1024, settings:{slidesToShow:1,slidesToScroll:1,infinite:true,dots:true} },
                   { breakpoint:600,  settings:{centerMode:false,infinite:true,slidesToShow:1,slidesToScroll:1} }]
    })
    Replicated below with vanilla CSS scroll-snap (single-slide track) +
    IntersectionObserver active-dot sync + click-to-scroll dot navigation.
    Skipped: slide cloning for swipe-past-end loop (slick adaptiveHeight reflow).

  Layout: source has the IMAGE as a full-section background <img>, with text overlaid
    on the LEFT half. We mirror by using a 2-column CSS grid with NO outer container
    (section is full-bleed). Image column flush to right edge. Text column padding-left
    pinned to where the 1300px page-max would start (so content aligns with the rest of
    the site's content rail) and padding-right gives the gap to the image edge.
